in
>the next few months ;-).

Perhaps there are two other possible solutions (actually ther are
incremental in a way).
1) Modify the DgnComp and LevComp to compare the dates of the source file
and destination file building the destination file from the source only
if the destination file is older.  In addition, have the desitination
file be in the right place (dungeon:dungeon, dungeon:*.lev, dungeon:data,
etc...).  No cost.  Just a hassel to update the compilers, run the
compilers, update NetHack.

2) Use AppleScript.  Think 6.0 supports a set of apple events that can be
use to build and run projects.  But this solution also costs $$.  But if
setup correctly, one script can do the hassel part of solution 1.

I really miss Unix and Makefiles :-(.

